// googl-bl.js — Alphabet Deep Dive ▸ Bottom Line ▸ General (BL-GEN-1…5) and Segments (BL-SEG), docs/PROFILE_PLAYBOOK.md §13.
//
// COPIED from js/overviews/meta-bl.js (itself tsm-bl.js → the dependency closure of amzn.js's aMarginsBody ·
// aBridgeBody · aNetBridgeBody · aSbcBody · expenseTabsBody · aBlFootGeneral · aBuildMargins · aBuildExpenses), then
// adapted to Alphabet — never reimplemented:
//   • data: ./googl-bbg.js (Bloomberg export, generated by scripts/bbg_extract.py) for the income statement and
//     consensus; ./googl-bl-data.js for the reported functional expense lines (10-K / 10-Q via SEC XBRL) and the
//     expense-line dives; ../results-data/googl.js for the quarterly operating-income series and the Summit series.
//   • expense lines = Alphabet's own (10-K MD&A): cost of revenues, split into its two reported parts — TAC and other
//     cost of revenues — then research and development · sales and marketing · general and administrative. They tie
//     to income from operations in every period.
//   • cost of revenues goes FIRST and apart in every bridge view, with a Gross profit subtotal (§13, SAB 2026-10-19),
//     and the bridge has the fourth mode "Cost structure" (stacked % of revenue over time).
//   • Consensus basis (SAB, Oct 26 2026): Bloomberg's headline revenue mixes brokers who forecast gross revenue with
//     brokers who forecast it net of TAC, so consensus revenue = the SUM of Bloomberg's segment lines (Services ·
//     Cloud · Other Bets · Alphabet-level hedging), as in the Results dataset, and every consensus margin is computed
//     on it. Consensus cost of revenues carries the same mix, so it is not shown; the forward bridge derives cost of
//     revenues as revenue − operating expenses − operating income, with TAC from the Services segment's consensus.
//     Gross profit IS shown (SAB, Oct 29 2026): it is TAC-neutral — a broker who nets TAC out of revenue also nets it
//     out of cost of revenues — and Bloomberg's GROSS_PROFIT runs at a ~60% margin on the segment-sum revenue.
//   • Normalized net income (SAB, Oct 26 2026) = GAAP − other income (expense), net, after tax at the period's
//     effective rate — Alphabet's GAAP earnings carry large unrealized gains on equity securities.
//   • Summit series: read from js/results-data/googl.js, where the Summit DCF model is FROZEN (rule 10 — coded from the
//     dated snapshot, not live). Every Summit chip says "frozen"; the footer names the snapshot, read off the data.
//   • Alphabet does not disclose SBC by income-statement line, so the SBC block shows the Dilution view only.
//   • Annex A fixed in the copy: no typed years or labels (A12); shares axis on the RIGHT (A9); no inline <style>
//     (A1/A10; styles in css/overview.css under :is(.ov-tsm-dd, .ov-meta-dd, .ov-googl-dd)); no hex colours (Summit
//     tokens from js/viz-palette.js); DOM lookups scoped to the Alphabet root, not document.
